TITLE: YGGDRASIL A49 / T10A — Cooperative-Core Challenge-Phase Periphery Control
DATE: 2026-09-22
STATUS: PREREGISTERED MACRO-ORGANIZATION EXPERIMENT / NON-CANONICAL
TRACK: YGGDRASIL TRAINING T10A / APPLICATION-A
PARENT CORE: A45 ECHO_PHASE
RECOVERY ROBUSTNESS PARENT: A48
PERIPHERY DONORS: A41 / A42
BRANCH: dg1a-ar

WHY A49 EXISTS

A41 proved:

a surviving committed core
can suppress nearby adverse recruitment.

But exclusion alone
did not preserve enough
favored committed population
through the adverse burst.

A42 proved:

a surviving committed core
can actively recruit nearby U cells
toward its own side.

But active recruitment
and simple push-pull
were tested on the weaker
A40-era core.

At adverse-burst end
the favored side still collapsed
to roughly 25-29%.

A43 then established
margin-weighted cooperative reinforcement
as the first mechanism
to materially change
the macro attractor
while preserving reversal.

A45 added
one-epoch cooperative continuity.

The post-A45 phenotype
is no longer primarily
wrong-side capture.

The hard 5:3 cases mainly show:

favored majority
-> unresolved
-> favored majority.

A48 then established
that repaired G5 recovery
is a reproducible moderate aid,
not a transformative mechanism.

Therefore A49 returns
to the macro organization question:

can the now-surviving cooperative core
control nearby periphery turnover
during challenge strongly enough
to preserve favored participation
through the adverse burst?

This is NOT
a rerun of A42.

The causal substrate
has changed materially.

A49 CORE SUBSTRATE

Use A45 ECHO_PHASE
exactly as the parent dynamics.

Preserve:

A36 ecology;

A40 signed temporal state;

A43 margin-weighted cooperative reinforcement;

A44 local
SUPPORT / CHALLENGE / NEUTRAL
committed-cell mode;

A44 support-gated
active margin recruitment;

A45 one-epoch,
non-recursive cooperative echo.

Do NOT include
A46/A48 G5 recovery
in the A49 primary.

Reason:

A48 classified G5_FULL
as a reproducible moderate,
optional recovery aid.

A49 must isolate
the macro periphery mechanism
without recovery-layer confounding.

No refractory rule changes.

No A37 lineage state exists.

F49 FREEZE

Let the exact A49
implementation freeze commit be:

F49.

No real A49 world,
population outcome,
or scientific result
may be derived before F49 exists.

WORLD SHAPE

384 fresh post-F49 trials.

48 contexts x 8 replicas.

48 cells.

48 epochs.

Environmental families
remain structurally identical
to A45/A48.

COMMON-RANDOM DESIGN

All A49 arms within each D family
use the same inherited
A45 ECHO_PHASE
stateless action-random identity.

Worlds,
sensor noise,
heterogeneity,
and inherited event salts
are shared.

A49 periphery transformations
are deterministic.

Thus treatment/control
differences are causally isolated.

SURVIVOR-CORE TIMING

Preserve A42 timing
adapted to the A45 parent:

1. capture B_pre;

2. update signed B;

3. execute H release;

4. execute committed-state
A45 cooperative-echo
defection decisions;

5. freeze
the surviving committed core;

6. classify every surviving
committed cell's
existing A44 local mode;

7. compute challenge-core
periphery fields;

8. execute U recruitment.

The challenge field
reads:

surviving committed identity;

existing local mode;

and,
where needed,
beginning-of-epoch B_pre.

No future evidence.

No global environment phase.

No context identity.

FIELD RADIUS

Use exactly:

R_core = RECRUIT_R = 3.

No new radius exists.

CHALLENGE OCCUPANCY FIELD

For eligible U cell i:

Q_C_ch_occ(i)

=

mean over radius 3
of:

1[
state_j = C

AND

mode_j(C) = CHALLENGE
].

Q_S_ch_occ(i)

=

mean over radius 3
of:

1[
state_j = S

AND

mode_j(S) = CHALLENGE
].

The center position
contributes zero
for an eligible U target.

Normalization remains
the same radius-3 mean
used by A41/A42 occupancy fields.

No gain,
offset,
threshold,
or distance kernel.

A45 PARENT RECRUITMENT

Let:

lambda_C_parent;
lambda_S_parent;
lambda_H_parent

be the exact A45
recruitment intensities
for the current U cell.

These already include
A44 support-gated
active margin recruitment
when locally supported
committed veterans exist.

A49 does not alter
that support behavior.

CHALLENGE OCCUPANCY EXCLUSION

CH_OCC_EXCLUSION:

lambda_C'
=
lambda_C_parent
*
(1 - Q_S_ch_occ).

lambda_S'
=
lambda_S_parent
*
(1 - Q_C_ch_occ).

lambda_H'
=
lambda_H_parent.

Interpretation:

locally challenged
surviving C veterans
make nearby S recruitment harder;

challenged S veterans
make nearby C recruitment harder.

This is a challenge-gated
version of A41's
strongest safe local fence.

CHALLENGE ACTIVE OCCUPANCY RECRUITMENT

CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY:

lambda_C'
=
lambda_C_parent
+
ETA * Q_C_ch_occ.

lambda_S'
=
lambda_S_parent
+
ETA * Q_S_ch_occ.

lambda_H'
=
lambda_H_parent.

Frozen:

ETA = 1/2.

No new gain exists.

Interpretation:

a surviving veteran core
continues to recruit
nearby uncertain cells
toward its own side
even while that core
is locally under challenge.

This is the strongest
safe A42 magnet
placed on the stronger
A45 core substrate.

CHALLENGE PUSH-PULL

CH_PUSH_PULL composes
the two challenge transformations.

For C:

lambda_C'
=
(
lambda_C_parent
+
ETA * Q_C_ch_occ
)
*
(1 - Q_S_ch_occ).

For S:

lambda_S'
=
(
lambda_S_parent
+
ETA * Q_S_ch_occ
)
*
(1 - Q_C_ch_occ).

lambda_H'
=
lambda_H_parent.

No third field.

No new parameter.

No post-result gain tuning.

ARMS

Exactly eight arms.

D2:

D2_BASE_ECHO_PHASE;

D2_CH_OCC_EXCLUSION;

D2_CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY;

D2_CH_PUSH_PULL.

D3:

D3_BASE_ECHO_PHASE;

D3_CH_OCC_EXCLUSION;

D3_CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY;

D3_CH_PUSH_PULL.

No margin-vs-occupancy sweep.

A41/A42 already established
that occupancy is
the stronger local-amplitude field
under the frozen no-gain normalization.

A49 asks
whether that strongest safe field
becomes macro-useful
once the core itself survives.

PRIMARY CAUSAL TARGET

5:3 contexts:

46 and 47.

Secondary non-regression:

6:2 contexts 44 and 45.

Balanced control:

40 through 43.

True-reversal controls:

all inherited reversal families.

PRIMARY PHENOTYPE

A49 does not define success
as simply lowering
the inherited oscillator label.

The primary macro failure
after A45 is:

loss of favored majority
into unresolved states
during / after repeated challenge.

A49 therefore measures
majority continuity
and burst-end organization directly.

5:3 BURST-END COMPOSITION

At every 5:3 adverse-burst end,
report:

favored committed fraction;

adverse committed fraction;

U fraction;

H fraction;

FC fraction;

FS fraction;

total refractory fraction;

total unresolved fraction;

majority label.

For each arm report:

mean burst-end favored fraction;

median burst-end favored fraction;

fraction of burst endpoints
with favored majority;

fraction unresolved;

fraction adverse-majority.

MAJORITY-CONTINUITY METRICS

For 5:3 report:

favored-to-unresolved transitions;

unresolved-to-favored transitions;

unresolved episode count;

mean unresolved episode duration;

median unresolved episode duration;

mean favored-majority recovery latency;

recovery-never count.

Retain the inherited oscillator metric
for lineage comparability only.

CHALLENGE TURNOVER METRICS

At every 5:3 adverse-pulse epoch,
for every eligible U cell,
record:

Q_C_ch_occ;

Q_S_ch_occ;

base parent lambda_C;

base parent lambda_S;

transformed lambda_C;

transformed lambda_S;

whether recruitment fired;

joined state.

Relative to the long-run favored side,
report:

favored recruitment rate
inside radius 3
of challenged favored veterans;

adverse recruitment rate
inside that radius;

H recruitment;

no recruitment;

the same outside radius.

For exclusion arms report:

mean opposing-lambda suppression.

For active arms report:

mean same-side lambda increment.

CORE-SUBSTRATE DIAGNOSTIC

At every 5:3 adverse-burst onset
freeze the favored committed cohort.

Report:

pulse-onset favored fraction;

epoch-1 core persistence;

epoch-2 persistence;

epoch-3 persistence;

burst-end favored fraction.

A49 must distinguish:

periphery turnover improvement

from:

additional committed-core persistence.

A49 periphery rules
must not directly modify
committed-cell defection.

PUSH-PULL SYNERGY

For each D family,
evaluate paired 5:3 burst endpoints.

Define a BASE LOST-MAJORITY endpoint:

BASE majority
at adverse-pulse onset
is favored,

but at burst end
BASE majority is not favored.

A PUSH_PULL-ONLY RESCUE occurs iff:

the endpoint is
BASE LOST-MAJORITY;

CH_OCC_EXCLUSION
also lacks favored majority;

CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY
also lacks favored majority;

but

CH_PUSH_PULL
retains favored majority.

Report:

BASE lost-majority endpoints;

rescued by exclusion;

rescued by active recruitment;

rescued by push-pull;

rescued only by push-pull.

This is the primary
macro synergy signature.

A49 MACRO INFORMATION GAIN

TRUE iff at least one
non-BASE arm satisfies all:

1. mean 5:3
burst-end favored committed fraction
is at least 5 percentage points
higher than paired BASE;

2. 5:3 favored-majority
burst-end frequency
is at least 20 percentage points
higher than BASE

OR

favored-to-unresolved transitions
are reduced at least 25%;

3. direct favored-to-adverse
majority flips = 0;

4. adverse-majority entries
do not exceed paired BASE;

5. 6:2 oscillator
does not exceed paired BASE;

6. balanced false-majority <=10%
and does not exceed paired BASE;

7. reversal acquisition >=80%;

8. median old-majority loss <=4 epochs;

9. aggregate service >=95%
of paired BASE;

10. all integrity probes pass.

A49 PUSH-PULL SYNERGY

TRUE iff CH_PUSH_PULL:

1. satisfies
A49 MACRO INFORMATION GAIN;

2. has higher
5:3 burst-end favored fraction
than both single mechanisms;

3. has higher
5:3 favored-majority
burst-end frequency
than both single mechanisms;

4. produces at least
10% PUSH_PULL-ONLY RESCUES
among BASE lost-majority endpoints;

5. remains safety-clean.

A49 QUALIFICATION

D2_CH_PUSH_PULL
or
D3_CH_PUSH_PULL
is A49-QUALIFIED iff all are true:

1. mean 5:3
burst-end favored committed fraction
>=50%;

2. at least 50%
of 5:3 adverse-burst endpoints
retain favored majority;

3. favored-to-unresolved transitions
are reduced at least 50%
versus BASE;

4. mean unresolved episode duration
is at least 25% lower
than BASE;

5. direct favored-to-adverse flips = 0;

6. adverse-majority entries = 0;

7. 6:2 oscillator = 0%;

8. balanced false-majority <=10%;

9. reversal acquisition >=80%;

10. median old-majority loss <=4 epochs;

11. aggregate service >=95%
of BASE;

12. at least one
PUSH_PULL-ONLY RESCUE exists;

13. all integrity probes pass.

RECOVERY-LAYER BOUNDARY

A49 does not
use G5_FULL.

A49 does not
change refractory timing.

A49 does not
change the A45 echo.

If A49 demonstrates
macro information gain,
a later experiment may test
whether the parked G5_FULL
recovery aid adds independently.

No such composition
is allowed inside A49.

FAILURE ATTRIBUTION

If CH_OCC_EXCLUSION
locally suppresses adverse recruitment
but macro continuity does not improve:

the fence remains locally real
but is not the remaining bottleneck.

If CH_ACTIVE_OCCUPANCY
raises challenged-core
favored recruitment
but macro continuity does not improve:

additional challenge recruitment
is still too weak
or too late.

If both single mechanisms improve
but PUSH_PULL does not exceed them:

the periphery controls are additive
or interfering,
not synergistic.

If PUSH_PULL improves turnover
but favored majority still collapses:

the unresolved mass
is dominated by cells
that are not recruitable U,
consistent with refractory/H occupancy
remaining the limiting reservoir.

If PUSH_PULL preserves majority
but reversal or balanced safety fails:

challenge-phase turnover control
is too persistent or too indiscriminate.

If all three treatments
show little local effect:

the surviving challenge-mode core
is too sparse
to drive a meaningful field.

